Known performance boundary
JSON parses and classifies once per changed document version; it does not maintain an incremental JSON AST. Cached reads reuse results; edits use minimal transport changes, typing stays local, and only visible rows are painted. A 2,117,747-byte / 56,940-line benchmark constructed from repository dependency metadata measured 128 ms initially, 12 ms cached and 108 ms after a partial edit. These are service-side measurements, not an end-to-end UI latency guarantee.

